// Nine full, exam-standard AgilePM v3 Foundation mock papers.
// Written to mirror the real APMG paper style: direct questions,
// "identify the missing word(s)", numbered-statement combination questions
// (1, 2, 3 / 2, 3, 4 ...) and two-statement true/false questions
// (Only 1 / Only 2 / Both / Neither).
//
// These papers are presented FIXED (no option shuffling) because several
// question types reference statement numbers or use "All of the above" — so
// correct answers are instead deliberately scattered across A-D, with no
// positional pattern. Every question is tagged with its syllabus area so the
// results screen can produce a strengths/weaknesses analysis.
//
// Content is grounded in the AgilePM v3 Foundation syllabus (Sept 2024) and
// the provided v3 reference material. Questions are original (written in the
// style of the exam), not copied from APMG's copyrighted question bank.

// Improvement guidance shown per syllabus area on the results screen.
export const TOPIC_TIPS = {
  KC: 'Re-read the Agile Manifesto (4 values + final sentence), VUCA, Business Agility, and the difference between product development and project management (syllabus 2.x).',
  SC: 'Lock down the Scrum definition, 5 values, 3 roles, 5 events + timeboxes, 3 artefacts + commitments, and the 3 pillars of empiricism (Scrum Essentials, 3.x).',
  AF: 'Memorise the 4 variables (fix Time/Cost/Quality, vary Features), the 8 principles, the philosophy quote, and how contingency is handled via MoSCoW (4.x).',
  IN: 'Drill the role accountabilities (Business Sponsor, Business Visionary, Solution Architect, Project Manager, Product Owner), Scrum Master duties, the PM\u2019s 6 and PO\u2019s 4 relationships, and the 9 leadership principles (5.x).',
  CC: 'Review collaboration vs communication definitions, communication choices (face-to-face vs email), the Power/Interest grid, and transparency (6.x).',
  PR: 'Know the 6 lifecycle phases and their purposes/work-products, plus the increment types (Product vs Solution vs Project) (7.x).',
  ES: 'Practise User Story format + 4 Cs + INVEST, MoSCoW rules and the 60%/20% effort guidance, estimating styles, and the Minimum Usable Subset (8.x, 9.x).',
  PC: 'Revise the 3 planning concepts, 4 tracking/control concepts, Management by Exception, Sprint structure, and the Project Planning Event inputs/outputs (10.x).',
  RK: 'Understand risk as a consequence of VUCA, risk ownership, and the Project Approach Questionnaire (purpose, timing, what to do on disagreement) (11.x).',
  GV: 'Nail the definitions of Governance and Empiricism, the Cone of Uncertainty, financial governance work-products, and assuring regulatory compliance (12.x).',
}

